ght: 25px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">15</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>\u00a0</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 175px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25.0499%; text-align: center; height: 25px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 74.9501%; text-align: center; height: 25px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Eligibility Criteria</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25.0499%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">DTE</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 74.9501%; height: 25px; text-align: left;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have an Engineering Diploma in Electrical / Electrical (Power) / Electrical &amp; Electronics / Power Systems Engineering / Power Engineering (Electrical). Minimum 70% marks are required for General, OBC (NCL), and EWS candidates, while SC, ST, and PwBD candidates only need to pass.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25.0499%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">DTC</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 74.9501%; height: 25px; text-align: left;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have a Diploma in Civil Engineering from any recognized technical board or institute in India. A minimum of 70% marks is required for General, OBC (NCL), and EWS candidates, while SC, ST, and PwBD candidates only need to pass.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25.0499%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">DTS</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 74.9501%; height: 25px; text-align: left;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have a Diploma in Survey Engineering or a Diploma in Civil Engineering with Survey as a subject from a recognized technical board or institute in India. A minimum of 70% marks is required for General, OBC (NCL), and EWS candidates, while SC, ST, and PwBD candidates only need to pass.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25.0499%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">JOT (HR)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 74.9501%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">\n<ul>\n<li data-end=\"372\" data-start=\"63\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have a regular Bachelor\u2019s degree in BBA, BBM, BBS, or an equivalent qualification from a recognized institute or university in India. A minimum of 70% marks is required for General, OBC (NCL), and EWS candidates, while SC, ST, and PwBD candidates only need to pass.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25.0499%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">JOT (F&amp;A)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 74.9501%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">\n<ul>\n<li data-end=\"268\" data-start=\"62\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates who have passed Inter CA or Inter CMA are eligible. Additionally, candidates with a Postgraduate Degree, Postgraduate Diploma, CA, or CMA qualification can also apply.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25.0499%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">JIT (Survey)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 74.9501%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">\n<ul>\n<li data-end=\"263\" data-start=\"62\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have an ITI (Surveyor) qualification from a recognized technical board or institute. For detailed eligibility conditions, refer to the official notification.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>\u00a0</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #800000;\">You May Also Check : <span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://sarkariresult.com.cm/chandigarh-clerk-steno-2026/\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\" target=\"_blank\">Chandigarh Clerk, Steno Recruitment 2026</a></span></span></strong></span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>\u00a0</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 100%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"background-color: #000080; color: #ffffff; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>\u00a0How To Check &amp; Download PGCIL Diploma Trainee Admit Card 2026\u00a0</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<ul>\n<li data-end=\"313\" data-start=\"256\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Open an\u00a0<strong data-end=\"284\" data-start=\"264\">internet browser</strong>\u00a0on your phone or computer.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"396\" data-start=\"317\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Go to the\u00a0<strong data-end=\"393\" data-start=\"327\">official website of the Power Grid Corporation of India Limited (PGCIL)</strong>.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"465\" data-start=\"400\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">On the homepage, find the\u00a0<strong data-end=\"454\" data-start=\"426\">Admit Card / Examination</strong>\u00a0section.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"558\" data-start=\"469\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Look for the notification named\u00a0<strong data-end=\"555\" data-start=\"501\">Diploma Trainee Admit Card 2026</strong>.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"604\" data-start=\"562\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Click to open the admit card login page.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"690\" data-start=\"608\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Enter your\u00a0<strong data-end=\"653\" data-start=\"619\">Registration ID or Roll Number</strong>\u00a0and\u00a0<strong data-end=\"675\" data-start=\"658\">Date of Birth</strong>\u00a0as required.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"757\" data-start=\"694\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Submit the details to view your\u00a0<strong data-end=\"740\" data-start=\"726\">admit card pdf</strong>\u00a0on the screen.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"873\" data-start=\"761\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Carefully check all details such as\u00a0<strong data-end=\"870\" data-start=\"797\">candidate name, roll number, exam date, time, and exam centre address</strong>.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"938\" data-start=\"877\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong data-end=\"908\" data-start=\"877\">Download the admit card PDF</strong>\u00a0and save it on your device.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"1013\" data-start=\"943\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Take a\u00a0<strong data-end=\"966\" data-start=\"950\">printed copy</strong>\u00a0of the admit card to carry to the exam centre.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>\u00a0</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 144px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 27px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 100%; text-align: center; height: 27px;\"><span style=\"background-color: #000080; color: #ffffff; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #ffffff;\">\u00a0PGCIL Diploma Trainee Recruitment 2026 : </span>Mode Of Selection\u00a0</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 117px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 100%; height: 117px;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><b>Written / CBT Examination</b></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><b>Skill Test</b></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Trade Test</strong></span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>\u00a0</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #cc0052;\">